Use direct replacement:

```ts
interface RegistrationMonth {
  start: string;
  amount: string | null;
  incomplete: boolean;
}

registrationTimeline(declarations: MemberDeclaration[])
// returns { months: RegistrationMonth[], undated: boolean }
```

The helper owns UTC calendar bucketing and month gaps. Normalize each timestamp with `setUTCHours(0, 0, 0, 0)` and `setUTCDate(1)`. Iterate normalized starts with `date.setUTCMonth(date.getUTCMonth() + 1)`. Starting on day 1 prevents January 31 overflow; UTC avoids DST; December rolls into January automatically.

Preserve the exact decimal summation and existing distinctions: empty months have `"0"`, months with only unknown amounts have `null`, and partially known months retain their known sum plus `incomplete: true`. Foreign-only entries do not extend the timeline or set `undated`.

Update both renderer props to `months`, rename the member-summary destructuring to `{ months: earnings, undated }`, and replace weekly copy in headings, SVG descriptions, tooltips and partial notes. Use the existing UTC month formatter for tooltips, preferably a long month name for clarity.

A configurable period adds unused weekly behavior and copy branching. Both consumers need monthly data, so one monthly contract is sufficient.

Verify boundary-offset timestamps, December/January, January 31 followed by leap February, missing months, exact aggregation within a month, and existing unknown/currency semantics.
